applicable missing, malformed, invalid-evidence, or trace diagnostics. Any `TDD_TEST_STALE` diagnostic uses the current trace test node's path rather than a historical cycle path. Evidence-array position, active-CHANGE filtering of candidate fingerprints, superseded coverage status, and legacy unscoped status do not override terminal fingerprint order for source-currency selection, so an older legacy unscoped cycle cannot shadow a later verified scoped cycle for an evaluated test. Array-position supersession classification remains outside this source-currency correction and does not determine the selected currency fingerprint. The changed source-currency work-event suppression and stale-diagnostic applicability, order-based applicability of retained `tdd void` messages, active-scope applicability and verified-selection precedence of retained migration messages, active-scope applicability of the void-fallback message, foreign-only exit-1 void result during an active CHANGE, trimmed migration-approver rejection and diagnostic applicability, and active-scope restrictions are intentional behavioral differences registered under REQ-M5-COMPAT-013 and ADR-0023. `TEST-M5-TDD-EFFECTIVE-LATEST-001` verifies the primary cross-CHANGE legacy/scoped verified-terminal ordering regression. `TEST-M5-TDD-MAINTENANCE-SCOPE-001` verifies the exact unverified-void no-overwrite exit-1 behavior. Unannotated companion cases in `tests/tdd-generation-scope.test.ts` supplement regression coverage for active and no-active membership and work suppression, migration selection and retained messages, void targeting and fallback, duplicate and invalid evidence, an out-of-scope cycle whose verified Green order is not strictly after its verified Red order being ineligible and supplying no terminal fingerprint or `TDD_TEST_STALE`, missing trace nodes, source-text and per-test fingerprint cache isolation, multiple test IDs in one source file, valid-void bounds, Refactor/migration precedence, and compat