Multi-Change-Create-Correction: Normative detail: the preceding sole-active confirmation-token rule remains unchanged in the control root. Inside a registered live candidate workspace, workspace ownership explicitly selects its CHANGE and positive generation before and after lease acquisition; the positional `<change-id>` remains a byte-exact confirmation token, another active CHANGE does not cause `CHANGE_GENERATION_MIXED`, and a token/workspace mismatch fails exit 1 `CANDIDATE_WORKSPACE_SELECTOR_MISMATCH` without persistence.

